# Wave W17-L (Route 103): wade sand — the path that gets its feet wet: damp pale sand running across the shallows, wet-sheened with bright water flecks where the surf keeps washing it (design-authorised pale sand running end to end across the water). The only path kind in the fleet that is drawn wet.
